mode: "100644"
text: "# Goals & Measurement\n\nA strategy needs one clear objective and an honest way to know if it's working. This is where\nbrands go wrong by chasing follower counts that never translate into anything.\n\n## Pick one primary objective (from what the business needs)\n\nSocial can serve different objectives; pick **one** primary (plus at most one secondary), driven\nby the business's actual stage and need:\n\n- **Awareness / reach** — get discovered. (Early brands, new products.)\n- **Audience growth** — build an owned following to nurture.\n- **Community / engagement** — deepen the relationship with existing followers.\n- **Authority / positioning** — become the name people associate with the topic.\n- **Leads** — capture interest (email, demo, DM, waitlist).\n- **Sales / conversion** — drive purchases directly.\n\nThe objective should map to the business: a pre-product startup usually needs awareness and\naudience; an established business with a funnel usually needs leads or sales. Don't default to\n\"more followers\" — ask what the *business* needs social to do.\n\n## Meaningful metrics vs vanity metrics\n\nChoose the metric that reflects the objective, and distrust the ones that just feel good:\n\n| Vanity (often) | Meaningful (usually) |\n|---|---|\n| Follower count | Saves, shares/sends |\n| Likes | Comments / DMs / replies |\n| Impressions alone | Profile visits → clicks |\n| \"Going viral\" once | Leads, sign-ups, sales, repeat reach |\n\nFollowers and likes matter only if they ladder up to the objective. A post with 200 saves and 10\nDMs usually beats one with 5,000 likes and no action. Pick a primary metric that would actually\nmove the business.\n\n## The funnel reality — social warms, it rarely closes\n\nSocial media mostly **warms** people through awareness → trust → consideration, and the\nconversion often happens elsewhere (site, email, DMs, sales call). So:\n\n- Don't judge a single post by direct sales; judge the *body of work* by the trust and demand it\n  builds.\n- Match the metric to where the channel sits in the funnel — awareness content is measured by\n  reach/saves, not purchases.\n- A \"conversion\" goal still needs upper-funnel content feeding it.\n\n## Honest measurement\n\n**WoopSocial publishes (measurement: the platforms' native analytics).** Measurement is\n**platform-native and manual** — read each platform's own insights, track your primary metric in\na simple sheet, and review periodically. Set targets, but:\n\n- Don't promise dashboards or automated reporting the product can't deliver.\n- Be wary of obsessing over numbers week to week; social compounds over months. Set a cadence to\n  review (e.g., monthly) rather than chasing every post.\n- To cascade the objective into SMART targets, per-channel North Stars, and action thresholds,\n  hand off to `goals-and-kpis`.\n\n## A simple goal statement\n\nWrite the objective as one line the whole strategy serves:\n\n> \"Over the next quarter, social exists to **{objective}**, measured primarily by **{metric}**,\n> on **{channel(s)}**.\"\n\nEverything else — pillars, plan, cadence — should be in service of that sentence.\n"
